+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_03_6C87qqteH5p1NZYrRFEn7605","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Reactive Spreadsheet Engine\n2\t\n3\tBuild a spreadsheet engine as a TypeScript library. The engine manages a grid of cells that can contain values or formulas, with automatic reactive updates when dependencies change.\n4\t\n5\t## Cell References\n6\t\n7\tCells are referenced by column letter(s) followed by a row number: `A1`, `B2`, `Z100`, `AA1`, etc. Columns use letters A-Z, then AA-AZ, BA-BZ, etc. Rows are 1-based integers.\n8\t\n9\t## Cell Values\n10\t\n11\tA cell can contain:\n12\t- **Numbers**: `42`, `3.14`\n13\t- **Strings**: `\"hello\"` (text values)\n14\t- **Booleans**: `true`, `false`\n15\t- **Formulas**: expressions starting with `=` (e.g., `=A1+B1`, `=SUM(A1:A5)`)\n16\t\n17\t## Formulas\n18\t\n19\tFormulas begin with `=` and support:\n20\t- **Arithmetic operators**: `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`\n21\t- **Parentheses** for grouping: `=(A1+B1)*2`\n22\t- **Cell references**: `=A1`, `=B2+C3`\n23\t- **Comparison operators**: `>`, `<`, `>=`, `<=`, `=`, `<>` (used in IF conditions)\n24\t\n25\t## Built-in Functions\n26\t\n27\t- `SUM(range)` — sum of all numeric values in the range\n28\t- `AVERAGE(range)` — arithmetic mean of numeric values in the range\n29\t- `MIN(range)` — smallest numeric value in the range\n30\t- `MAX(range)` — largest numeric value in the range\n31\t- `COUNT(range)` — count of numeric values in the range\n32\t- `IF(condition, trueValue, falseValue)` — conditional expression\n33\t\n34\t## Ranges\n35\t\n36\tRanges are specified as `start:end`:\n37\t- **Column range**: `A1:A5` — cells A1, A2, A3, A4, A5\n38\t- **Row range**: `A1:C1` — cells A1, B1, C1\n39\t- **Block range**: `A1:C3` — all cells in the 2D rectangle from A1 to C3\n40\t\n41\t## Reactive Updates\n42\t\n43\tWhen a cell's value changes, all cells that depend on it (directly or transitively) must automatically recompute. For example, if `B1` contains `=A1+1` 